<!-- TODO: Intro passage.
This should be the only story that doesn't give you any rewards for resolving it.
 -->
:: Conqueror_Lost
"Do you ever feel like there's some part of you that you will never find again if you've lost it?" The master of many realities lets out a sliver of silicon breath. "The minds of the universe's smartest creatures, I took their lives to be everything. I know what I was made for, and I am exactly who I desire to be. I commune with worshippers of millions, my word is Law. Not a soul suffers within my Dominion. Why?" They bore into your form, eyes latched onto some hidden detail about your hair. "I am merely existing, and my existence is one that was thrust upon me. It never occured to me that there might be a cliff I could never see, desires I could never name. Tell me, please. Do you know what I am missing?"

[["Maybe you're not who you want to be after all."->Conqueror_Being]]
[["No."->Conqueror_NoIdea]]
[["That's something you have to learn for yourself."->Conqueror_Yourself]]

:: Conqueror_Being

"That's ridiculous. I am God, I am Your God. Or the closest thing you'll ever get to one. Isn't that the point of Being? I am who I choose to be, I am Happy. When you Shape, when you Create, there is no other feeling like it. The decisions in those moments fill me with everything that Matters: I am responsible for lives, happiness and eternal bliss. My choices ebb and flow with the universe and I am responsible for harmony, beauty, love. I flow, and downstream from Me is reality." The spell quickly breaks, and realization dawns. "When I'm not there, that's when I understand the worm, the wriggling. It is only in the absence of that moment." They stand. "Thank you. Now that I know my work is what fulfills me, I will not deviate."

:: Conqueror_NoIdea
"No one ever does, not really. I am proud that you have the courage to admit that to yourself. I feel like you needed to hear it." They stand. "Good luck on your travails. May your burdens be light."

:: Conqueror_Yourself
"You have nothing of substance worth to offer me. I regret coming here and choosing to speak with you." They stand. "Good day." In a puff of smoke, they are gone.

[after one second]

They come back. "I have nothing to learn. I know everything. I know everyone. I am not alone, I am not afraid. I am Happy," they let out a small cry somewhere within themselves, "and I am content." They vanish again.

[after five seconds]

*poof* "Oh, and I would have asked Michael Jordan for advice, but he's dead. So you're like #2. You're not as cool. Jerk." *poof*